# decimal_subtract_refund — exact money subtraction via Decimal (README §27/§30.5,
# X-093). Money/Decimal is a scaled Int64 (scale 2: the raw value is amount*100),
# so a $15.75 charge minus a $5.25 refund leaves $10.50, computed EXACTLY as
# 1575 - 525 = 1050 with `decimal.subtract` — no binary-float rounding error.
#
# Correctness observation: 1575 - 525 == 1050 ($15.75 - $5.25 = $10.50).
# Expected output: PASS lines + `---- 2 passed, 0 failed ----`

DecimalSubtractRefund is project
DecimalSubtractRefund module examplesDecimalSubtractRefund
DecimalSubtractRefund target console
DecimalSubtractRefund entry main

examplesDecimalSubtractRefund is module
examplesDecimalSubtractRefund path examples.decimalSubtractRefund
examplesDecimalSubtractRefund exports main
examplesDecimalSubtractRefund purpose "Subtract a refund from a charge exactly with Decimal"
examplesDecimalSubtractRefund invariant "Scaled-integer money subtracts without float error"

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32

Decimal is alias
Decimal for Int64
Decimal purpose "Fixed-scale money: the raw Int64 is the amount * 100 (scale 2)"

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout

main is operation
main out ExitCode
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memory heap no
main async no
main purpose "Compute $15.75 - $5.25 exactly and assert $10.50"
main invariant "Writes the test harness summary"
main let charge immutable Decimal 1575
main let refund immutable Decimal 525
main let harnessName immutable String "decimal_subtract_refund"
main let harnessExpected immutable Decimal 1050
main let noopDecoy immutable Decimal 0
main let noopName immutable String "decimal_subtract_refund: real remainder (not the no-op 0)"
main do subtractRefund
main do writeResult
main do noopCheck
main do harnessReport
main return harnessSummaryCode

subtractRefund is call
subtractRefund in main
subtractRefund invokes decimal.subtract
subtractRefund arg left Decimal charge
subtractRefund arg right Decimal refund
subtractRefund out remaining Decimal

writeResult is call
writeResult in main
writeResult invokes test.assertEqualInt64
writeResult arg name String harnessName
writeResult arg expected Int64 harnessExpected
writeResult arg actual Int64 remaining

noopCheck is call
noopCheck in main
noopCheck invokes test.assertNotEqualInt64
noopCheck arg name String noopName
noopCheck arg expected Int64 noopDecoy
noopCheck arg actual Int64 remaining

harnessReport is call
harnessReport in main
harnessReport invokes test.summary
harnessReport out harnessSummaryCode ExitCode
